1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,200
MyCampusView Academy. Robotics 101, video 1: Welcome to Robotics 101.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,642
Hello and welcome!

3
00:00:06,692 --> 00:00:12,842
In this course you will build a small robot that can follow

4
00:00:12,892 --> 00:00:17,150
a black line on the floor, all by itself.

5
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:23,751
Here is the robot you will build, shown in our simulator.

6
00:00:23,801 --> 00:00:29,016
It has two eyes underneath that look at the floor.

7
00:00:29,066 --> 00:00:34,280
When the line bends, the robot turns to follow it.

8
00:00:34,330 --> 00:00:36,597
Nobody is steering it.

9
00:00:36,647 --> 00:00:39,650
The robot decides on its own.

10
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:43,695
Robots like this are used in real life.

11
00:00:43,745 --> 00:00:47,846
Warehouse robots follow lines to carry parcels.

12
00:00:47,896 --> 00:00:54,117
Some hospitals use them to deliver medicines, and factories use them to

13
00:00:54,167 --> 00:00:57,650
move parts from one machine to the next.

14
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:00,916
The course has four modules.

15
00:01:00,966 --> 00:01:03,487
First, you meet your robot.

16
00:01:03,537 --> 00:01:06,819
Next, you learn how its parts work.

17
00:01:06,869 --> 00:01:09,390
Then you write the program.

18
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:14,150
Finally, you build it, test it and make it better.

19
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:18,297
Every lesson follows the same pattern.

20
00:01:18,347 --> 00:01:24,270
You watch a short video, try an activity or the simulator, check

21
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:30,150
what you learned with a few questions, and then build and test.

22
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:35,402
Do not worry if you do not have a robot kit yet.

23
00:01:35,452 --> 00:01:41,896
Every lesson works in your browser, and the simulator lets you test

24
00:01:41,946 --> 00:01:43,350
the same ideas.

25
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:49,650
You can even complete the final challenge on the virtual pathway.

26
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:51,402
Safety first.

27
00:01:51,452 --> 00:01:55,388
Always ask an adult before you use batteries.

28
00:01:55,438 --> 00:01:59,374
Never let the battery wires touch each other.

29
00:01:59,424 --> 00:02:05,309
Unplug the power before you change any wires, and keep your fingers

30
00:02:05,359 --> 00:02:09,650
away from the wheels when the motors are running.

31
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:16,572
By the end, you will have a working robot, a certificate, and

32
00:02:16,622 --> 00:02:20,303
six badges to collect along the way.

33
00:02:20,353 --> 00:02:21,650
Let us begin!

34
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:28,500
Next: Understanding robots: sense, think, act.
